v {xschem version=3.4.4 file_version=1.2}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
template="name=x1"
description="The sampler, wired to the source: design/xschem/sampler_core.sch's ro_array_core (N = 4 five-stage rings, DR-0003) plus six sampler_dff instances -- raw_bit, raw_valid, and ring_bit1..ring_bit4. Pin order MUST track design/xschem/sampler_core.sch's own .subckt signature exactly: en1..en4 vddr1..vddr4 vdd vss clk rst_n raw_bit raw_valid ring_bit1..ring_bit4 -- see design/sampler_core.spice. ring_bit1..4 are the per-ring digitized samples a liveness monitor consumes, one per ring so no ring is unmonitored, produced by four more instances of the same sampler_dff cell on ro_array_core's ro1..ro4 observation outputs; like raw_bit they are digital block-internal signals, and unlike raw_bit they are not a tap anyone reads off-die. Instantiated by trng_top.sch as the analog half of the top-level assembly; raw_bit/raw_valid is the raw tap and the analog/digital verification-level boundary."
}
V {}
S {}
E {}
